{
    "background_story": "In the late 19th century, Poppy was a notorious highbinder, a term used to describe a labor organizer and union leader. Born into a family of dockworkers, she saw firsthand the exploitation and mistreatment of workers on the waterfront. Poppy became determined to fight for their rights and better working conditions. With her charisma and persuasive abilities, she rallied workers and formed a powerful union. Her fearless leadership and strategic thinking helped the union win key battles against corrupt employers and politicians. Poppy's reputation as a fierce highbinder spread, earning her the respect and admiration of workers across the city. Her legacy continued to inspire future generations of labor leaders and activists.",
